# Consciousness criteria, content presentations and epistemic interpretation

Architectural indicators and context-respecting realization provide operational
criteria. Rooted relational content presentations give a candidate structural
vocabulary for phenomenal interpretation; partial sections describe its exposed
features. Component bases connect such descriptions to the existing
two-dimensional scrutability and information-state theories without assuming a
global that's-all truth.

Pain and joy at the selected event, global sustaining separation and formation
carriers, arbitrary additional features, and assessor-indexed quantitative
appraisals remain distinct. Event-indexed additional qualities belong to the
enriched presentations and constrain their arrows. A report adjunction concerns
partial descriptions; it does not identify their carriers with subjects or their
gluing with the combination of experiences. Experiential interpretation and
correspondence with physical or deployed implementations require separate
justification.

Interpretation-relative assessments retain jointly supported candidate outcomes
and distinguish global outcome support from coverage of every admitted
interpretation. Provenance-indexed ledgers connect typed report evidence to
compatible operational states. Complete chronological profiles retain episodes
that endpoint and multidimensional totals can erase. Workspace receipt queries
give an operational currency assay with explicit stale-evidence controls.
-/
